.TH doubletake-ctl 1 "November 2026" "doubletake" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
doubletake-ctl \- Control doubletake daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B doubletake-ctl
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGUMENTS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B doubletake-ctl
is a command-line interface for controlling the
.B doubletake
daemon. It manages simultaneous mirroring and audio-only sessions and reports their status.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
List active connections with their transport, timing protocol and playout leads.
.TP
.B discover
Refresh receiver discovery.
.TP
.B devices
List cached discovered receivers.
.TP
.B connect [\fITARGET\fR] [\fIPIN-OR-PASSWORD\fR]
Start streaming to a receiver, optionally supplying a PIN or password. If no
target is specified, connect to the first available discovered receiver.
.TP
.B play \fISOURCE\fR [\fITARGET\fR]
Play video and audio from a local file or a direct HTTP(S) media URL until end of input.
With no target, use the
first available discovered display. To stop early, use \fBdisconnect\fR.
.TP
.B pin \fIPIN-OR-PASSWORD\fR
Submit the credential for a receiver waiting for input. The command retains its
historical name for compatibility: the pending value may be either an on-screen
PIN or a configured receiver password. Exactly one receiver must be waiting;
when multiple receivers are waiting, use
.B connect \fITARGET\fR \fIPIN-OR-PASSWORD\fR
to select one explicitly.
.TP
.B disconnect [\fITARGET\fR]
Stop streaming to a receiver. If no target is specified, disconnects all active connections.
.TP
.B mute [\fITARGET\fR]
Mute receiver audio for one receiver, or all receivers if no target is supplied.
.TP
.B unmute [\fITARGET\fR]
Unmute receiver audio for one receiver, or all receivers if no target is supplied.
.TP
.B volume \fITARGET\fR [\fIDB\fR]
Read the receiver's volume during playback, or set a value between
\-30 and 0 dB. Use mute and unmute to toggle sound. Setting a level while
muted saves that level for unmute.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-socket \fIPATH\fR
Override the daemon control socket (default: $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/doubletake.sock,
or /tmp/doubletake.sock when XDG_RUNTIME_DIR is unset).
.TP
.B \-version
Show the version and source commit, then exit.
.TP
.B \-help, \-h
Show command-line help and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Check daemon status:
.B doubletake-ctl status
.TP
Connect to an Apple TV:
.B doubletake-ctl connect 192.168.1.77
.TP
Connect to multiple Apple TVs:
.B doubletake-ctl connect 192.168.1.77
.B doubletake-ctl connect 192.168.1.100
.TP
Disconnect from a specific Apple TV:
.B doubletake-ctl disconnect 192.168.1.77
.TP
Disconnect all connections:
.B doubletake-ctl disconnect
.SH USAGE
First, start the doubletake daemon in a separate terminal or background:
.IP
.B doubletake \-daemonize
.IP
Then use
.B doubletake-ctl
to manage connections:
.IP
.B doubletake-ctl status
.B doubletake-ctl connect 192.168.1.77
.B doubletake-ctl connect 192.168.1.100
.PP
The JSON returned by
.B status
uses
.B needs_credential
to report pending input and
.B credential_kind
to distinguish
.B pin
from
.BR password .
The legacy
.B needs_pin
field remains true only for an actual on-screen PIN.
.PP
Each waiting connection is also listed in
.B streams
with its own target and credential kind, allowing concurrent prompts to be
completed independently.
.SH SHELL COMPLETION
Bash completion for commands, options, and socket paths is included in release
packages and source installations. Install the
.B bash-completion
package and start a new shell to load it automatically.
.SH SEE ALSO
.B doubletake(1)
